{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31899 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is implicated in the regulation of A2780cisR through a series of molecular interactions involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a target for multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A and Pseudopterosin Q, which are themselves targets of Nortoxiferine, dihydro-. The observed pathway suggests that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- exerts its biological effect by modulating the activity of the 26S proteasome, which is a key component in the cellular degradation of proteins. This mechanism is supported by the presence of a specific compound, [(1S,2R,4S,5R,8R,10S,13R,14R,17S,18R)-2-hydroxy-4,5,9,9,13,20,20-heptamethyl-24-oxahexacyclo[15.5.2.01,18.04,17.05,14.08,13]tetracosan-10-yl] acetate, which is also a target of Nortoxiferine, dihydro- and ultimately affects A2780cisR. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Nortoxiferine, dihydro- in influencing cellular processes through the proteasome, with implications for the regulation of A2780cisR. The evidence suggests a direct and mechanistic link between Nortoxiferine, dihydro- and A2780cisR, mediated through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14.",
